re_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00228,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.083,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":8.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"CG Oncology, Inc., a late-stage clinical biopharmaceutical company, develops and commercializes cretostimogene grenadenorepvec for patients with bladder cancer in the United States. The company's product candidate is cretostimogene, an investigational oncolytic immunotherapy, which is in phase 2 clinical trials of cretostimogene in patients with high-risk NMIBC after BCG failure; a phase 3 clinical trials to evaluate the safety and efficacy of cretostimogene as monotherapy in the treatment of patients who have received adequate BCG therapy with high-risk BCG-unresponsive, CIS-containing NMIBC and BCG-unresponsive Ta, or T1 papillary tumors; phase 3 BOND-003 Cohort C trials as a single agent; phase 3 BOND-003 Cohort P as a single agent in patients with BCG-UR papillary-only NMIBC. It also develops cretostimogene monotherapy for intermediate-risk NMIBC following TURBT, which is in phase 3 PIVOT-006 clinical trials to assess the safety and efficacy of adjuvant cretostimogene; and cretostimogene monotherapy for high-risk NMIBC in phase 2 CORE-008 clinical trials to assess the safety and clinical outcomes of cretostimogene in treating patients with high-risk NMIBC, including BCG-exposed and BCG-na\u00efve NMIBC. The company was formerly known as Cold Genesys, Inc. and changed its name to CG Oncology, Inc. in June 2020. CG Oncology, Inc. was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Arthur  Kuan | President, Chairman & CEO | Age 34 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 142 people. Revenue per employee of $28K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $188K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 40\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["CG Oncology, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $6.7B market cap on $4M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +255% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -1417% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $132M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -1852.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 2.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 660% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 4722% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.26499889307062197},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (92% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.083},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 222% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Large open-market insider purchases (net $20.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CG Oncology\u2019s loss widens 29.9% and trial data is due in November (NASDAQ: CGON)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/cg-oncologys-loss-widens-29-9-and-trial-data-is-due-in-november-nasdaq-cgon.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999724.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CG Oncology, Inc. (CGON) Reports Q3 Loss, Beats Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025553/cg-oncology-inc-cgon-reports-q3-loss-beats-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3025553","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973301.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags"